    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1303">

                <pb facs="1130" n="816" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg816"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 855.48/36</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Herrick</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1914-11-11">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">November 11, 1914</hi>.</date>
                    <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 5:40 p.m.</hi>] </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>267. Your 253, 10th. Foreign Office states that instructions have already been
                    sent French Minister at The Hague to offer no objection to transit of foodstuffs
                    through the Netherlands from United States destined to Belgium. At Embassy’s
                    request Foreign Office stated it would repeat instructions to Minister at The
                    Hague.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Herrick</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
